      {
        "AlertId": "112148",
        "Headline": "State/Lake Elevated Station Temporary Closure",
        "ShortDescription": "Effective, now, the State/Lake Loop Elevated station is closed for reconstruction into 2029. Please use adjacent stations at Clark/Lake or Washington/Wabash.",
        "FullDescription": {
          "#cdata-section": "<p><strong>How does this affect my trip?</strong><br />\r\nEffective, Monday, January 5, 2026, the State/Lake Loop Elevated&nbsp;station will temporarily close.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlease use the accessible Clark/Lake or Washington/Wabash&nbsp;stations, located within a few blocks of the State/Lake station. To&nbsp;transfer between the Red Line at Lake station and the Loop &lsquo;L&rsquo; lines,&nbsp;use Washington/Wabash.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Why is service being changed?</strong><br />\r\nThe new State/Lake elevated station is scheduled to open in 2029. It&nbsp;will replace one of the oldest stations on the CTA rail system with a&nbsp;modern facility designed to improve safety, accessibility, and comfort&nbsp;for all riders.</p>\r\n"
        },
        "SeverityScore": "12",
        "SeverityColor": "000000",
